WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:07.320
One of the reasons that it is crucial that
everybody just stay home is that many people

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:12.590
have the virus but have no symptoms or almost
no symptoms and what are sometimes called

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:17.190
asymptomatic or sometimes maybe more accurately,
subclinical cases.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.199
And the question has been, to what degree
is this a thing?

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:26.529
We've heard numbers thrown out that suggest
anywhere from as little as 5 or 10 percent

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:32.489
of the population that's infected all the
way up to 50 percent may be asymptomatic or

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:34.030
at least subclinical.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:39.730
And Iceland has been testing this pretty precisely
with some large numbers of tests which they

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.489
can do thanks to their small population.

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:45.980
Iceland's total population is under 400000
people total.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:52.260
And the latest results from a study of 9000
people in Iceland is that as many as half

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:59.620
of those infected have no idea because they
have no symptoms noticeable enough for them

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.020
to perceive those.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.289
So what Iceland did is Iceland did a test
of about five, has had so far tested about

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:08.840
5 percent of its population, just pretty broad
testing.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.999
That's about 18000 tests.

00:01:10.999 --> 00:01:16.640
And then there's been a separate testing protocol
which has tested 9000 people who chose to

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.640
participate.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.979
Fewer than 1 percent of the tests came back
positive, meaning that the percentage of the

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:26.399
population, in fact, that is believed to be
under 1 percent.

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:31.049
But half of the positive tests were people
who said, I never had any symptoms.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.389
I've felt fine the entire time.

00:01:33.389 --> 00:01:38.399
And yet they if they're not home, which many
in Iceland are not, because Iceland actually

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:41.409
has not done the stay at home part very seriously.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:43.619
You were out spreading the disease.

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:47.680
If you are out and about, this is why everybody's
got to stay home.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.560
The asymptomatic spread appears to be absolutely
huge.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.939
Now, understand that even though this this
nine thousand person test was randomized,

00:01:55.939 --> 00:02:02.219
it is made up of people who are choosing to
get tested.

00:02:02.219 --> 00:02:04.299
And that could impact the results in some
way.

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:07.669
But imagine it's not 50 percent and it's 20
percent or 15 percent.

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:13.240
If 15 percent of the cases that are out there
are asymptomatic and people don't know it,

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:17.870
that's why it's important to stay home regardless
of how you feel, regardless of your age or

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.870
anything else.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:19.950
We're working together.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.439
We're trying to get past this.

00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:29.280
And this result also reinforces the eventual
importance of having a simple at home antibody

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.349
test, which could answer the question, did
I ever have coronavirus?

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:40.299
Now, the FDA did yesterday approved the first
antibody test, the serology test.

00:02:40.299 --> 00:02:43.500
It is a blood test, but it's not a pinprick
test.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.129
It's a vein test.

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:46.129
You would.

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:50.209
Once this gets rolled out, you would have
to go into a lab to have the tests done.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:54.290
How many of those tests were likely to do
under that protocol to test the population?

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.790
I don't really know.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:00.450
But we are going in the direction of being
able to test for antibodies, which is a very

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.590
good thing.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:07.709
Often when people post to social media and
say, you know, I think I might have had this

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:10.319
a month ago, a month and a half ago, whatever.

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.650
It's very popular to shame those people and
to say stop being dramatic.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.159
Almost everybody who has it has a fever.

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:21.799
And that's true of symptomatic patients who
have been tested.

00:03:21.799 --> 00:03:25.900
If you don't have symptoms, you obviously
don't have a fever.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:05:34.930
And when we get eventually to the point where
we can start opening back up a little bit.

